  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nRainbow oscillation decomposition generates structured overlap patterns, leverages gradient-based optimization, and includes broad exploration strategies to escape local optima. This addresses the high-dimensionality and non-convexity of the Er\u0151s minimax overlap problem.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\n- h(x) represented as piecewise constant step function [0,1] on [0,2]\n- Various evaluations across scales using rainbow sequences and smooth approximations\n- Objectives defined at different resolutions with smooth loss functions to approximate the max correlation\n\n3. Implementation procedure\n- Single resolution implementation prioritizing spectral optimization\n- Rainbow sequence generation\n- Gradient approximation and projection\n- Local search via harmonic entrainment\n- Objective evaluation using smooth max\n- Hybrid methods with multiple resolution layers\n\n4. Search choices and variations\n- Default: Rainbow oscillation with harmonic alignment\n- Variants: \n  - Graphite oscillation (smoother)\n  - Ammonite (increased local variation)\n- Adaptive resolution\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\n- Greedy implementation tradeoff between resolution and optimization time\n- Scalable updates with fallbacks to periodic function\n\n6. Validation and return contract\n- Objective validation at different scales\n- Progress via level-set optimization\n- Robust fallback to periodic structure",
